        "type": "text",
        "text": "Understood — design the build pipeline so DMG+notarization (A) can drop in later, but expect day-to-day reality to be ad-hoc builds shared directly (C) until there's a Developer ID. That doesn't change anything structural, just means the export/naming/versioning should be tidy from the start so builds are shareable.\n\nThat was a note on distribution though — I still need your read on **Part 1 (the architecture)** from my last message:\n\n- Record-time: capture every selected source as its own WAV stem, non-destructively, all started on one trigger\n- Export-time: pick tracks post-session, mix/group/export as M4A or WAV\n- Per-app capture via Core Audio process taps (macOS 14.4+), mic as a source alongside\n- Five modules: `RecorderEngine`, `SourceRegistry`, `SessionStore`, `ExportEngine`, and the two UI faces\n\nDoes that architecture look right to you? Any part you'd question — e.g., always-record-everything-selected vs. mixing decisions at record time?"
