        "type": "text",
        "text": "No problem at all — that just settles it cleanly: **ad-hoc builds for now** (friends right-click → Open the first time, which is a one-time friction), and the moment you get a Developer ID later, we add notarization to the build script and it becomes a proper DMG. Zero architecture impact, so consider distribution closed.\n\nBack to the still-pending question — **does the Part 1 architecture look right?**\n\nQuick recap of what you're approving:\n\n1. **Record time:** every selected source (Chrome, Zoom, mic, …) captured as its own WAV stem in a session folder, all started on one trigger, non-destructive (audio keeps playing normally — no BlackHole-style rerouting)\n2. **Export time:** pick tracks post-session, export combined / grouped / individually as M4A or WAV\n3. **Capture:** Core Audio process taps per app (macOS 14.4+ floor), mic as a normal source alongside\n4. **Modules:** `RecorderEngine` (only file touching Core Audio), `SourceRegistry`, `SessionStore`, `ExportEngine`, menu bar + main window UI — with the future seams (tab extension as a source type, transcription as an export target) already in the boundaries\n\nAnything you'd question, or shall I move on to Part 2 — the UI and edge cases?"
